nvk-nak-stats: NAK_STATS=1 prints one JSON line per compiled shader stage on stderr (3.0.14).
NullMoth's own change (not an upstream Mesa commit).

Phase 0 of the compiler work: an instrument that changes nothing. Every later change to NAK is judged by the same
figures over the same shaders (tools/nak-corpus, compared with tools/nak_stats_diff.py), so the compiler has to say
them in a form a script reads. NAK already counts most of them (NAK_DEBUG=print writes them as text, and Vulkan's
pipeline executable statistics show them); what it did not count is how many instructions run on the uniform data
path, and nothing wrote them one shader per line.

With NAK_STATS=1 (read once per process) nak_compile_shader_internal writes, after the shader is finished and before
it is encoded, {"nak_stats":1,"stage":..,"sm":..,"blake3":..} followed by instrs, instrs_warp, instrs_uniform, gprs,
warps_per_sm, static_cycles, spills_to_mem, fills_from_mem, spills_to_reg, fills_from_reg and slm. instrs_uniform
counts the instructions whose destinations are uniform registers (Instr::is_uniform, the test opt_uniform_instrs uses);
instrs_warp is the rest. gprs is the count Vulkan's statistics show (hardware-reserved registers included, at least 4).
blake3 is the hash of the shader's SPIR-V. A compute shader that NAK builds twice reports the build it keeps.

Unset, or set to anything but 1, nothing is read from the shader and nothing is written. The switch changes no code,
so it is not part of the shader cache key: a shader that comes from a cache is not compiled and prints nothing, which
is why tools/nak-corpus/run.sh turns the caches off.
diff --git a/src/nouveau/compiler/nak/api.rs b/src/nouveau/compiler/nak/api.rs
--- a/src/nouveau/compiler/nak/api.rs
+++ b/src/nouveau/compiler/nak/api.rs
@@ -535,6 +535,38 @@
     fn drop(&mut self) { NVMTL_RA_BUDGET.with(|v| v.set(self.old)); }
 }
 
+/// nvk-nak-stats: NAK_STATS=1 (read once per process) turns on the per-shader JSON line.
+fn nak_stats_on() -> bool {
+    static ON: OnceLock<bool> = OnceLock::new();
+    *ON.get_or_init(|| env::var("NAK_STATS").map_or(false, |v| v == "1"))
+}
+
+/// nvk-nak-stats: one JSON object on one line, {"nak_stats":1,"stage":"..","sm":N,"blake3":"<hex>",then each field}.
+/// The stage keeps only letters, digits and '_', and the field names are fixed by the caller, so nothing needs
+/// escaping. blake3 is the hash of the shader's SPIR-V (all zero for a shader that did not come from SPIR-V).
+fn nak_stats_line(
+    stage: &str,
+    sm: u8,
+    blake3: &[u8],
+    fields: &[(&str, u64)],
+) -> String {
+    let mut out = String::with_capacity(360);
+    out.push_str("{\"nak_stats\":1,\"stage\":\"");
+    out.extend(stage.chars().filter(|c| c.is_ascii_alphanumeric() || *c == '_'));
+    out.push_str("\",\"sm\":");
+    out.push_str(&sm.to_string());
+    out.push_str(",\"blake3\":\"");
+    for b in blake3 {
+        out.push_str(&format!("{:02x}", b));
+    }
+    out.push('"');
+    for (name, value) in fields {
+        out.push_str(&format!(",\"{}\":{}", name, value));
+    }
+    out.push('}');
+    out
+}
+
 fn nak_compile_shader_internal(
     nir: *mut nir_shader,
     dump_asm: bool,
@@ -626,6 +658,46 @@
         }
     };
 
+    // nvk-nak-stats (3.0.14): NAK_STATS=1 prints one JSON line per compiled shader on stderr, for the corpus runs of
+    // tools/nak-corpus and tools/nak_stats_diff.py. It reads the finished shader and changes nothing in it.
+    if nak_stats_on() {
+        let mut uniform: u64 = 0;
+        s.for_each_instr(&mut |instr| {
+            if instr.is_uniform() {
+                uniform += 1;
+            }
